  "infoBulletsB1": "Spot spending habits at a glance.",
  "infoBulletsB2": "Plan ahead before the month starts.",
  "infoBulletsB3": "Know exactly where every dollar goes.",
  "infoBulletsB4": "Build confidence with your finances.",
  "infoBulletsB5": "Be ready for surprise expenses.",
  "infoCard1Body": "A budget tells your money **where to go** so you stop wondering **where it went**. Think of it as a game plan for every dollar you earn.",
  "infoCard1Title": "The Big Idea",
  "infoCard2Body": "Start with your **net income** (what actually hits your account). Then create **categories** like groceries, rent, fun money, and savings. Assign dollars to each one until you hit zero.",
  "infoCard2Title": "How It Works",
  "infoCard3Body": "The magic number is **zero**. Income minus categories should equal zero. That doesn’t mean you spend it all, it means **every dollar has a purpose**, even the ones going to savings.",
  "infoCard3Title": "Every Dollar Gets a Job",
  "infoCard4Body": "The **horizontal bar** at the top shows how each category **fills up your income**. It’s a quick visual snapshot of where your money is going, no math needed.",
  "infoCard4Title": "Your Progress Bar",
  "infoCard5Body": "Each category shows how much is left. If it’s **green**, you’re on track. If it turns **red**, you’ve gone over, time to shuffle things around or take note for next month.",
  "infoCard5Title": "Green & Red Signals",
